(Page 2 of 3: Ohm's Law and Kirchhoff's Laws) Tj
0 -30 Td
(1. Ohm's Law: The potential difference V across a conductor is proportional to current I.) Tj
0 -25 Td
(2. Kirchhoff's Current Law (KCL): The sum of currents entering a node equals zero.) Tj
0 -25 Td
(3. Kirchhoff's Voltage Law (KVL): The sum of potential drops around a closed loop is zero.) Tj
0 -25 Td
(4. Thevenin's Theorem: Linear two-terminal circuits can be reduced to Vth and Rth.) Tj
